[[include info:start]]
**SCP-9352:** Autopsy Anomaly
**Author:** [[*user aismallard]] ([[[aismallard|Author Page]]])

**Thanks to:**
* [[*user Ralliston]]
* [[*user stormbreath]]
[[include info:end]]

**Item #:** SCP-9352

**Object Class:** Safe

**Special Containment Procedures:** SCP-9352 is kept in the Anomaly Wing of the Site-17 Morgue. Physical analysis or inspection is prohibited.

**Description:** SCP-9352 is a cadaver. The object's physical properties cannot be confirmed due to its anomalous nature.

Every autopsy performed on SCP-9352 has yielded a different result when performed by a different organization. Subsequent inspections (including casual observation) has yielded information equivalent to that organization's original report.

**Discovery:** The US FBI's [[[unusual-incidents-unit-hub|Unusual Incidents Unit]]] learned of abnormalities over the course of a murder investigation. The initial report, carried out by the county, was of a body that did not match the description of the murder victim, as described by a witness (who later could not be found for further questioning). Law enforcement then requisitioned a private autopsy, which produced a contradictory report. It was at this point that federal containment officials intervened.

Upon taking SCP-9352 into custody and performing their own autopsy, the UIU found that their report significantly differed as well. At this point, the Pittsburgh Foundation Liaison reached out to see if Foundation resources could be of assistance.

Foundation investigators produced their own, incompatible report regarding the nature of SCP-9352, and per agreement with UIU officials, brought it into containment.

**Addendum 9352-1:** Autopsy Reports

> **Designation:** SCP-9352-1
> 
> **Organization:** Allegheny County Medical Examiner
> 
> **Medical Examiner:** Robert G. Masterson
> 
> ----
> 
> **External Inspection:** 5'10" (178 cm) male, age estimated in the 40s. No external injuries or trauma. In particular, no bullet wounds could be identified.
> 
> Appearance significantly diverges from Jim Barber, as described in the murder report.
> 
> **Internal Inspection:** No signs of internal injury. No apparent cause of death.
> 
> **Notes:** For unknown reasons, this individual was dressed as a police officer at the time of his death. To date, the corpse has not been identified.
> 
> **UIU Interview Results:** Inconclusive. No evidence of anomalous activity during the autospy.

> **Designation:** SCP-9352-2
> 
> **Organization:** Wang & Wang Forensics
> 
> **Medical Examiner:** Bo Wang
> 
> ----
> 
> **External Inspection:** 6'2" (189 cm) obese white male, age estimated in the 50s. Weight recorded as 247 lb (112 kg). Recovered wearing eyeglasses designed for strong myopia. I-shaped incision from prior autopsy not present. No bullet wounds visible.
> 
> Like SCP-9352-1, this instance significantly differs in appearance from Jim Barber.
> 
> **Internal Inspection:** Healthy but higher-than-average levels of formaldehyde in the blood. Cause of death recorded as dehydration.
> 
> **UIU Interview Results:** Inconclusive. Because Bo Wang could not be located, his brother and business partner Lai Wang was interviewed instead.

> **Designation:** SCP-9352-3
> 
> **Organization:** Federal Bureau of Investigation, Unusual Incidents Unit
> 
> **Medical Examiner:** Jennifer Puckett
> 
> ----
> 
> **External Inspection:** Male of East Asian descent, 5'3" (160 cm), 103 lb (47 kg). No evidence of I-shaped incision from prior autopsy. Severe bruising on knuckles, arms, and legs (post-mortem, unknown cause).
> 
> **Internal Inspection:** High levels of cortisol in blood. Evidence of chronic liver disease. Cause of death eventually determined to be hypovolemic shock.
> 
> **Notes:** Report noted "significant difficulty" in making incisions due to "awkward placement" of limbs, eventually ameliorated by securing the deceased with belts. Subject made unidentified noises throughout first half of procedure.
> 
> **UIU Interview Results:** Reported a strong suspicion that the anomaly was observation-based. Follow-up inspection has seemed to substantiate this, however further testing could not be conducted as Jennifer Puckett was reported AWOL soon after. Foundation and UIU operatives are attempting to track her.

> **Designation:** SCP-9352-4
> 
> **Organization:** SCP Foundation
> 
> **Medical Examiner:** Shankar Choudhury
> 
> ----
> 
> **External Inspection:** White female, height of 179 cm, weight of 70 kg. No evidence of I- or Y-shaped incisions from prior autopsies. Found wearing a lab coat.
> 
> **Internal Inspection:** Moderate liver damage due to alcohol abuse. Microchip implant behind left shoulder blade.
> 
> **Laboratory Data:** No matches for DNA, fingerprint, dental, or retinal scans in Foundation or FBI databases. The discovered microchip was identical in design to those implanted into UIU personnel, however it did not contain a valid personnel file ID.

